license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/sonosk/sonosk"
url: "https://sonosk.github.io/sonosk/"
abstract: >-
  SonoSK is a Python library for simulating medical ultrasound. It models
  transducers from single elements to linear, phased, convex, matrix and
  focused arrays, computes continuous-wave pressure fields with the
  Rayleigh integral and the angular spectrum method, simulates pulse-echo
  signals and B-mode images of numerical phantoms, solves the Pennes
  bioheat equation for focused ultrasound exposures with thermal dose and
  lesion maps, models piezoelectric stacks with the Mason circuit, and
  reports acoustic output indices and image quality measures.
keywords:
  - ultrasound
  - simulation
  - medical imaging
  - transducer
  - beamforming
  - HIFU
  - focused ultrasound
  - bioheat
  - thermal dose
  - acoustic output
